# WHITNEY · differential motion as a light score, after John Whitney Sr., Digital Harmony (1980)
@prompt twelve lights at whole-number speeds lock into a figure; a detune lets the figure breathe
@world lab bpm=120 haze=0.03
@cast glass:glass at=0,0,0
@cast veil:veil at=-3,0.5,-1
@cast golden:golden at=3,-0.4,-1
@light Permutations intensity=1.4
@camera orbit dist=10 speed=0.6
@source whitney basis="theme only" title="Digital Harmony (1980); Permutations (1968); Matrix III (1972); Arabesque (1975)"
@ekphrasis 0s..8s "Permutations: every light turns at a whole multiple of one speed, so the figure locks"
@op 8s light Matrix detune=0.004
@ekphrasis 8s..16s "a small detune: the lights slip out of phase, and the figure breathes"
@op 16s light Arabesque
@op 16s camera beneath dist=6 follow=glass
@ekphrasis 16s..24s "wheels on wheels: a light crossing a bell makes it beat"
@test 24s beats glass >= 1
@test 24s visible glass
@test 24s fps > 1
